                "source": "Twitter for iPad",
                "text": "So Trump/Musk just announced 50% cut in workers at Social Security to cut the deficit btw already short staffed . \ud83e\udd14. Social Security and Medicare admin overhead is about 2% compared to private Medicare advantage plans at 28%. All the costs of administrating Soc Sec and Medicare are paid from FICA - social security taxes - that means no deficit savings. But good luck if a Soc. Sec recipient has a problem with their initial legitimate application  or those on Soc Sec disability already a 2 year wait .  Trump/musk/Vance and their cronies do not give a shit about the 70 million soc sec recipients or the 5.6 million who paid in their whole life who will become eligible next year.",
